  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers, and potentially a few thunderstorms, \nlikely late this weekend into early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA cold front approaches our area Saturday night with an area of\nlow pressure developing along it Sunday. The low should pass \nnorth of our area Sunday night into Monday. Showers and an \nisolated thunderstorm possible, mainly over northern and \nwestern Maine, Sunday afternoon as the cold front approaches. \nThe majority of the rain is expected Monday as the low passes to\nour north with a 30 to 40% chance of at least 0.5 inches \nDowneast and a 60 to 70% chance of at least 0.5 inches over the \nNorth. Rain tapers off Monday night. The greatest chance for \nthunderstorms is also Monday but it is unclear how widespread \nthey will be and how far south they will extend. Models are \ncurrently showing limited instability and more southerly flow \nalong the coast could bring a marine layer inland which would \ngenerally stunt convection. Fog likely each night through Sunday\nnight and may persist into the morning. Densest fog expected \nSaturday night.",
